      "prompt": "In △ABC, side BC is extended to point D. m∠A = 52° and m∠B = 71°. Find the exterior angle m∠ACD.",
      "figure": {
        "alt": "Triangle ABC with side BC extended past C to D. Angle A is 52 degrees, angle B is 71 degrees, and exterior angle ACD is marked x.",
        "pts": [
          { "id": "A", "x": 6.0, "y": 266.0, "name": "A" },
          { "id": "B", "x": 194.8, "y": 266.0, "name": "B" },
